    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0118" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 14503/39A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Argentine
                    Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-04-05"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inform you of the appointment by
                    the President of Maj. Gen. Leonard Wood as special ambassador of the United
                    States of America to the centenary celebration of the Argentine Republic.</p>
                <pb facs="0119" n="7" xml:id="pg7"/>
                <p>Gen. Wood, accompanied by his aid-de-camp, Capt. John R. Procter, will sail for
                    Buenos Aires on the 8th instant by the U. S. cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Montana</hi> and should reach their destination about the middle of
                    May.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Huntington Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
